2026-01-28 17:22:24,937 [DEBUG] voyage - data='{"input": ["Delighted to host dinner for a delegation led by my friend Mme. Delphine Benassy, Vice President of the Regional Council of R\\u00e9gion Centre-Val de Loire (France), in the backdrop of an MoU being signed between Centre-Val de Loire and our Hon\\u2019ble Chief Minister mkstalin This reflects not only the deepening ties between TN and France, but also our shared aspirations for greater collaboration and friendship in the years ahead.", "A clip from my interview with TimesNow, reflecting on my grandfather P. T. Rajan\\u2019s role in consecrating the new Lord Ayyappa idol at Sabarimalai in the 1950s\\u2014and popularising the pilgrimage across South India. These actions embodied the Justice Party and Dravidian movement\\u2019s vision of social inclusion and faith accessibility, building on values that had already led to the nationalisation of the erstwhile Kingdoms\' Temples in the 1920s.", "It\'s a settled fact in AI/ML that high-quality data alone is insufficient; sophisticated models require humans in the loop for training and evaluation. I saw this principle brought to life in Aranya Sahay\\u2019s brilliant and meditative film, Humans in the Loop.", "The film tells the story of Nehma, a first-generation Adivasi woman working as a data annotator in her Jharkhand village. It draws a remarkable parallel between her work training AI and the process of raising a child. As she grapples with real-world prejudices reflected in the models she trains, the film holds a mirror to our society and the future we are building. This film is based on a real-life woman worker at iMerit\\u2019s Ranchi centre; it resonated deeply, especially after I had the privilege of", "deeply, especially after I had the privilege of inaugurating iMerit\'s Coimbatore centre last year.", "Humans in the Loop is a thought-provoking film that reveals the vast, hidden workforce behind AI. It jolts us into an awareness of the pervasive biases we 